// =============================================================================
// financing-debt-course — "Financing: The Debt You Sign and the Lender You Face"
// =============================================================================
// Course seven of the Real Estate department. Six courses covered the ground,
// the stewardship, the transaction, the tenant, the building and the partner.
// This one covers the money that made all of them possible, and the party on
// the other end of it.
//
// THE ARC, one argument in eight moves:
//   1. The head and the tail (Deuteronomy 28:12, 43, 44)
//   2. When the money failed (Genesis 47:15, 19, 20, 23, 26)
//   3. They shall rise up suddenly (Habakkuk 2:6, 7)
//   4. The wicked borroweth, and payeth not again (Psalms 37:21, 25, 26)
//   5. What hast thou in the house (2 Kings 4:1, 2, 3, 4, 7)
//   6. Usury, and who your brother is (Deuteronomy 23:19, 20)
//   7. Alas, for it was borrowed (2 Kings 6:5, 6, 7)
//   8. He frankly forgave them both (Luke 7:41, 42, 43)
//
// Know the position you took -> see how a position becomes a surrender in
// reasonable stages -> price the one thing borrowers misprice, which is time ->
// find where the Word actually locates the fault -> answer pressure with
// production rather than with another arrangement -> learn which loans may
// never be priced at all -> handle a thing that is not yet yours -> and finish
// where Jesus finishes the subject, which is not repayment.
//
// THE LINE THIS COURSE HOLDS (DR-0098). Scripture nowhere forbids borrowing,
// and this course invents no prohibition Yahweh did not give. Lesson 1 says so
// explicitly, because a congregation taught that debt is sin will HIDE it, and
// a hidden position cannot be worked. What the Word gives instead is harder and
// more useful: a position (28:44), a mechanism (Genesis 47), a timing warning
// (Habakkuk 2:7), and a fault located precisely at "payeth not again" rather
// than at "borroweth" (Psalms 37:21). Lesson 6 keeps both halves of the usury
// command together, since either half quoted alone produces a false teaching.
//
// THE DEPARTMENT'S RECURRING SHAPE, a seventh time: a wrong invisible from
// inside any single instance. The false weight, the lawful process that took
// Naboth's vineyard, attrition on a promise, the seating chart, the daub, the
// disagreement never stated -- and now the chain of individually reasonable
// trades in Genesis 47, and the deferred service on a financed thing that is
// not entirely yours to neglect.
//
// WHERE THE COURSE REFUSES TO FLATTER (DR-0100). Genesis 47 ends with Pharaoh
// taking a fifth and the people retaining four fifths, which is a better ratio
// than a great many modern arrangements. Lesson 2 says so plainly rather than
// darkening the text to make its warning land harder.
//
// NO PASSAGE IS SHARED with any of the department's other six courses, and the
// course test CHECKS that against their own reference lists. All eight
// book-and-chapters are fresh ground against the 73 already in use.
//
// BANDS, BENEFITS AND STORIES FROM THE FIRST COMMIT (DR-0509). Every lesson
// carries levels.teen and levels.senior (DR-0497/0498), six `benefits`, and two
// `stories`, so neither the send stage nor the teach stage can render a heading
// with nothing under it.
//
// VERIFICATION (DR-0076 / SCRIPTURE-REFERENCE-STANDARD). All 108 quoted spans
// fetched VERBATIM from the repository's own KJV, and the generator refuses to
// emit while any span, ellipsis-in-a-quotation, straight apostrophe or
// capitalised adversary remains. Our prose says Yahweh; quotations keep "God"
// and "the LORD" exactly as the KJV has them (DR-0210's bright line).
//
// TEACHING, NOT LEGAL OR FINANCIAL ADVICE -- carried on the meta. Loan terms,
// disclosure rules, foreclosure procedure, bankruptcy and the enforceability of
// any particular clause are jurisdiction specific and they change.
// =============================================================================

